cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  This archive holds the code, data and notebooks behind the analyses of the article below.
  To apply DDSA to your own line lists, use the Julia package DiscreteDynamicSurvivalAnalysis.jl.
type: software
title: "Discrete dynamic survival analysis of epidemic case line lists: code and analyses"
version: 1.0.1
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23924833
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/epirecipes/DDSA-manuscript"
abstract: >-
  Code, notebooks and supplementary analyses used for the manuscript "Discrete dynamic survival
  analysis of epidemic case line lists": a synthetic outbreak under three data-availability
  scenarios, a comparison with ODE count models, the 2009 H1N1 outbreak at Washington State
  University, the 2018-2020 Ebola epidemic in the DRC and the 1861 measles outbreak in Hagelloch.
  To apply DDSA to other line lists, use the package DiscreteDynamicSurvivalAnalysis.jl.
keywords:
  - dynamic survival analysis
  - epidemic modelling
  - line lists
  - Bayesian inference
  - Julia
authors:
  - family-names: Montes-Olivas
    given-names: Sandra
  - family-names: Frost
    given-names: Simon D. W.
